      <activity id="dda213fe-132a-55dc-b773-ec9143fed09e" activityNameId="48ba16eb-8668-5731-af56-f17bc2b239e6" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, SOFC, allocated by exergy, distributed by pip [70e0210e63]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, SOFC, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, PEM using electricity from grid
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, SOFC. The hydrogen is produced by  Electrolysis, PEM, with electricity from grid as feedstock. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 33%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 120. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 268.75. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 90. Lifetime [years]: 19.51. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.08. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 5fee7485-9f7d-3dfa-b414-c457dac4131c
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_5fee7485-9f7d-3dfa-b414-c457dac4131c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
